q BT 65.20 771.39 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.246 Tw (Don had said, "These things happen, my dear," in the voice of a man who knew exactly how) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 750.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (they happened.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 721.50 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.582 Tw (Because the Don had ordered it. Isabella's brother had been investigating the Costa family. The) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 701.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.143 Tw (Don had him removed, the way he removed problems. And Isabella had stood in the rain and) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 680.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (smiled that same small, strange smile, and said nothing at all.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 651.20 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.244 Tw (She waited a year. She waited for the birthday dinner, when everyone would be watching the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 630.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (food, and no one would be watching the glasses.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 601.31 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (But there was one more thing Marco remembered, and it was the thing that saved his life.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 571.83 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.310 Tw (Enzo the sommelier had been nervous all night. His hands shook when he poured. And after the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 551.42 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.102 Tw (Don died, Marco had seen Enzo slip a second bottle out of the dining room and hide it in the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 531.01 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (cellar -- a bottle with no label, that had never been on Marco's wine list.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 501.53 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (There had been TWO murders planned at that table.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 472.05 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.546 Tw (The Don had ordered Enzo to poison the glass of Carmine, the rival sitting across the table, the) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 451.64 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.184 Tw (man the Don had been planning to kill for months. The poison was for Carmine. Isabella had) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 431.23 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.762 Tw (simply switched the glasses -- the Don's glass for Carmine's -- and the Don had drunk his own) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 410.83 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (murder.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 381.35 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.182 Tw (Two poisons. One table. And the only man who knew both halves of it was the chef, standing in) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 360.94 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (a wine cellar, with Roberto's men waiting for an answer.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 331.46 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (Marco looked at Roberto, the dead Don's son, and he made his choice.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 301.98 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.819 Tw ("The poison was not in my food," he said. "It was in the glass. And the glass was switched by) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 281.57 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (your wife -- because your father killed her brother, and she waited a year to answer him.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 252.09 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.095 Tw (Roberto stared at him for a long time. Then he did something Marco did not expect. He laughed.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 231.68 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (A short, broken sound.) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 202.20 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.053 Tw ("My father killed her brother," Roberto said quietly. "I know. I have known for a year. And I did) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 181.79 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (nothing.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 152.31 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.584 Tw (He turned to his men. "Let the chef go," he said. "And tell my wife -- tell Isabella -- that she is) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 131.90 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 0.189 Tw (free to leave this house tonight. I will not stop her. What my father did to her family, this family) Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 111.49 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg (owed her an answer for.") Tj ET Q
q BT 65.20 82.01 Td 0.0784 0.0784 0.0784 rg 1.183 Tw (Marco walked out of the wine cellar and into his kitchen for the last time. He took his recipe) Tj ET Q
